# Therefore, to grant the correct functioning and processing of the file in R, we altered the line ending of the 2 copied files, that could be in DOS (Windows). In our case, "ClusterTabSeparated.txt" was, in fact, in DOS. Thus, we used the command "vi" that opens a new interface, followed by ":set ff=unix". What this does is change the line ending to Unix, a more efficient line ending that simplifies coding and prevents conflicts in cross-platform development.
~/repeatexplorer/lupinus$ vi ClusterTabSeparated.txt
:set ff=unix
:wq
~/repeatexplorer/lupinus$ vi COMPARATIVE_ANALYSIS_COUNTS.csv
:set ff=unix
:wq


